**Bug found and fixed.**

The bug was on line 43 of `src/sim.ts`:

```ts
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {  // was: >= 0
```

The condition used `>=` which triggered population growth even when food production exactly equaled consumption (`foodSurplus == 0`). The docstring says population should only grow on a *surplus*, which means strictly greater than zero.

**Fix:** Changed `>=` to `>` so population only grows when `foodProduced > foodConsumed`.

All 4 tests pass.


